    </p>
    <p>
      There are other options, like "byte pair encoding", but the those chunks are even less coherent. However, there is one simple tweak to our algorithm that will take our tokenization from good to great. We do basically the same thing as described above, but we essentially add a penalty to chunks made of individually common words. This is called the "unigram" language model. Here is what that gives us:
    </p>
